<h2>Segment 238 &mdash; personal and collective karma</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s238S">de la <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w1">rma bya</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s238w2">la sogs pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w3">mdongs</span> la sogs pa <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w4">sna tshogs pa</span> ni, sems can de rnams kho na&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w5">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w6">thun mong ma yin pas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w7">skyed pa</span>&#x27;o, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w8">pad ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s238w9">la sogs pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w10">&#x27;dab ma</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s238w11">dang</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w12">kha dog</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w13">sna tshogs pa</span> ni, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w14">sems can</span> gyi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w15">thun mong</span> gi <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w16">las</span> kyis <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w17">bskyed pa</span>&#x27;o, , de bzhin du <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w18">gzhan</span> la&#x27;ang shes par bya&#x27;o</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s238S">On this subject, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w4">intricate</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w3">patterns</span> on a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w1">peacock</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s238w2">and other such</span> objects are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w7">produced</span> by each one&#x27;s <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w6">personal</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w5">karma</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w13">intricacies</span> of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w10">petals</span> <span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s238w11">and</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w12">colors</span> of a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w8">lotus flower</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s238w9">and other such</span> things are <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w17">produced</span> by the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w15">collective</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w16">karma</span> of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w14">living beings</span>. You can apply these principles to all <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s238w18">other</span> cases as well.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first proposal. The two productive events have separate karma/produced occurrences. The first sems can de rnams kho na'i is distributed across each one's and personal and is omitted, not nulled. The second la sogs pa after mdongs has no confidently separate closing gesture and is omitted; the first and third la sogs pa own only and other such, excluding supplied objects/things. mdongs owns patterns and sna tshogs pa owns intricate; the later sna tshogs pa owns intricacies. The case-bearing compound thun mong ma yin pas remains whole; its instrumental ending is not split off. The final knowing/applying instruction is a distributed recast: only gzhan/other is retained. No claim is made for supplied all, cases, principles, or the passive auxiliaries.</div>
